    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "€1,285 a month, not €1,252. One small rate rise on a variable mortgage.",
        "start": 0.27,
        "seconds": 8.03,
        "window": 8.63,
        "fill": 0.93
      },
      {
        "scene": "headline",
        "text": "In September, the European Central Bank raised its deposit rate to 2.5%. It decides again this month.",
        "start": 8.9,
        "seconds": 6.7,
        "window": 7.17,
        "fill": 0.934
      },
      {
        "scene": "source",
        "text": "Up from 2.25%. It is what banks earn on cash parked at the ECB.",
        "start": 16.07,
        "seconds": 4.81,
        "window": 5.33,
        "fill": 0.902
      },
      {
        "scene": "list",
        "text": "When it moves, savings follow slowly and partly. Variable loans follow at their next reset. Fixed loans don't move.",
        "start": 21.4,
        "seconds": 6.07,
        "window": 6.63,
        "fill": 0.916
      },
      {
        "scene": "save",
        "text": "On €10,000 saved, 2% pays €200 a year. 2.25% pays €225.",
        "start": 28.03,
        "seconds": 7.85,
        "window": 8.4,
        "fill": 0.935
      },
      {
        "scene": "rohan",
        "text": "So my loan can move faster than my savings?",
        "start": 36.43,
        "seconds": 2.04,
        "window": 2.53,
        "fill": 0.806
      },
      {
        "scene": "lesson",
        "text": "Often. So know if your loan is variable, and when it resets.",
        "start": 38.97,
        "seconds": 3.06,
        "window": 3.53,
        "fill": 0.867
      },
      {
        "scene": "outro",
        "text": "Then the news won't catch you out.",
        "start": 42.5,
        "seconds": 1.63,
        "window": 1.97,
        "fill": 0.827
      }
    ]
  },
